 and Kuadrant subsystems without direct API dependency. [source: internal/controller/services/auth/auth_controller.go:56-88]\n\nSecurity enforcement follows a defense-in-depth pattern: admission webhooks validate and default DataScienceCluster and DSCInitialization resources with a fail-closed policy, the metrics endpoint uses Kubernetes authentication and authorization filters when secure serving is enabled, and all webhook traffic is encrypted via OpenShift service-ca provisioned TLS certificates. The operator builds with `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime` and `CGO_ENABLED=1`, ensuring FIPS-compliant cryptographic primitives on RHEL hosts. [source: Dockerfiles/Dockerfile.konflux:56-59, cmd/main.go:483-494]\n\n## Provenance\n\n### Repo Lineage\n\n| Role | Repository | Sync Mechanism | Sync Branch | Sync Workflows | Detection Method |\n|----|----------|--------------|-----------|--------------|----------------|\n| Upstream | https://github.com/opendatahub-io/opendatahub-operator | auto_merge | rhoai | -- | sync_config |\n| Downstream | https://github.com/red-hat-data-services/rhods-operator | auto_merge | rhoai | `bundle-sync.yml`, `sync-main-to-stable.yaml`, `sync-stable-to-rhoai.yaml`, `trigger-gitops-sync.yaml` | local_analysis |\n\n### Aliases\n\n| Current Name | Previous Name | Type | Context |\n|------------|-------------|----|-------|\n\n## Architecture Components\n\n| Component | Type | Purpose |\n|---------|----|-------|\n| Dockerfiles/Dockerfile.konflux:ENTRYPOINT | Container entrypoint | [\"/manager\"] |\n| Dockerfiles/Dockerfile:ENTRYPOINT | Container entrypoint | [\"/manager\"] |\n| cloudmanager | Go executable | cmd/cloudmanager |\n| cmd | Go controller-runtime operator | cmd |\n| component-codegen | Go executable | Go entrypoint |\n| data-science-prometheus-cluster-proxy | Controller-created Deployment | kube-rbac-proxy ({image}) |\n| data-science-prometheus-namespace-proxy | Controller-created Deployment | kube-rbac-proxy ({image}), prom-label-proxy ({