{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d62d049b-1404-4f27-b1c5-8acac7fa8989","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-963ef9aa591f413f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-im2hhlpv/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E002.md","content":"# Standardize cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic applies the same structured-logging standardization to the rhods-operator's cloudmanager binary, which handles multi-cloud infrastructure dependencies (deployed on AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave). Its reconciliation controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) are built on the same controller-runtime/logr foundation using the shared reconciler pattern, so they already receive `name`/`namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger; the remaining work is converting message-embedded resource identity in error paths and adding `resourceKind`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the cloudmanager binary's controllers using grep/static analysis; produce a coverage checklist of every call site and whether it embeds resource identity in the message string.\n- Convert every reconciliation error log call in the cloudmanager binary that embeds resource name or namespace in the message string to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in the AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, and CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine controllers.\n- Handle cluster-scoped resources if present in these reconciliation paths: emit `name` and `resourceKind`; `namespace` is either omitted or set to empty string, never a spurious value.\n- Author and verify the CI lint rule / static-analysis check covering the cloudmanager binary's converted call sites: it flags any `log.Error` call in the cloudmanager binary that embeds name/namespace in the message text or is missing the required structured fields.\n- Backwards-compatibility validation (per the strategy's NFR): before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error, and verification that the production log consumers used on the non-OpenShift Kubernetes deployments ingest the new format without configuration changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Every reconciliation error log call in the cloudmanager binary that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string now uses structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) — measured by the coverage checklist (every audited call site accounted for) and the CI lint rule flagging zero remaining violations in the cloudmanager binary.\n- Unit tests assert that AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, and CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields with correct values, verified by parsing test logger output.\n- A unit test confirms cluster-scoped resources in these paths do not emit a spurious namespace value (namespace omitted or empty string).\n- The CI lint rule / static-analysis check covering the cloudmanager binary's call sites is authored, committed, and passes on the converted codebase (zero violations), and fails on a deliberately non-compliant call site.\n- The before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error is recorded, showing structured fields present alongside the changed message text, and log consumer ingestion is verified without configuration changes.\n- Existing unit tests in the cloudmanager binary pass with the log changes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): convert message-embedded resource name/namespace to structured KV pairs — cloudmanager binary call sites.\n- HLR-5 (P0): cloudmanager controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":36936,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b10400d4ddc10d55","agent_id":"a94e80975625d5b70","session_id":"ddc88db0-c91c-4182-8c51-a0cdf64bc03d","uuid":"aade6b8e-6d9e-4c85-9783-daa233f1ae6c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:33:30.943Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
