{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b425d8cff74d4afc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 8\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic converts all reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator manager binary to structured key-value pairs so operators can query logs by resource name, namespace, and kind. It addresses the three diagnosed problems within the manager binary: message-embedded resource identity (converting e.g. `log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile Foo in namespace bar\")` to `log.Error(err, \"reconciliation failed\", \"name\", foo.Name, \"namespace\", foo.Namespace, \"resourceKind\", \"Foo\")`), the DSCI controller's non-standard key names (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` migrated to `name`/`namespace`), and the missing `resourceKind` field across all controller tiers. Field naming follows camelCase to align with controller-runtime's existing structured log key conventions.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager binary using grep/static analysis; produce a coverage checklist of every call site and whether it embeds resource identity in the message string (this audit also confirms the strategy's 75% embedded-identity assumption).\n39\t- Convert every reconciliation error log call in the manager binary that embeds resource name or namespace in the message string to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n40\t- Migrate the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller from non-standard key names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) to the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`).\n41\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in all manager-binary controller tiers:\n42\t  - DSC controller (DataScienceCluster) and the 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI) — where kind is implied by controller name, this is a queryability enhancement added in the same pass.\n43\t  - Module controller and its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator).\n44\t  - 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) — kind is not implied by controller name for these.\n45\t  - DSCI controller.\n46\t- Add `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields to error logs in all 15 action files across 4 tiers: 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), 3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n47\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): emit `name` and `resourceKind`; `namespace` is either omitted or set to empty string, never a spurious value.\n48\t- Author and verify the CI lint rule / static-analysis check covering the manager binary's converted call sites: it flags any `log.Error` call in the manager binary that embeds name/namespace in the message text or is missing the required structured fields.\n49\t- Backwards-compatibility validation (per the strategy's NFR): before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error; deploy a test build to a dev cluster with the production log consumer stack configured (Loki, CloudWatch), trigger reconciliation errors, and verify both formats are ingested without configuration changes; coordinate with SRE/Support to identify text-based alert rules that rely on the changed message strings and record the identified rules and needed updates.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Every reconciliation error log call in the manager binary that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string now uses structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), and the redundant identity is removed from the message text — measured by the coverage checklist (every audited call site accounted for) and the CI lint rule flagging zero remaining violations in the manager binary.\n54\t- All DSCI controller structured field names use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`); a grep of the codebase confirms no references to the old field names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization` as log keys) remain, and a unit test asserts DSCI error logs contain the standard field names.\n55\t- For each service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup), a unit test parsing test logger output asserts `resourceKind` is present with the correct value on reconciliation errors.\n56\t- Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with correct values in error logs across all 15 action files (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module).\n57\t- Unit tests assert module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` across all 8 module handlers.\n58\t- Unit tests assert DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`.\n59\t- A unit test confirms cluster-scoped resources do not emit a spurious namespace value (namespace omitted or empty string).\n60\t- The CI lint rule / static-analysis check covering the manager binary's call sites is authored, committed, and passes on the converted codebase (zero violations), and fails on a deliberately non-compliant call site.\n61\t- The before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error is recorded, showing structured fields present; the dev-cluster validation with the production log consumer stack confirms ingestion of both formats without configuration changes; the SRE/Support coordination on text-based alert rules is completed and its results recorded.\n62\t- Existing unit and end-to-end tests in the manager binary pass with the log changes.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-1 (P0): convert message-embedded resource name/namespace to structured KV pairs — manager binary call sites.\n67\t- HLR-2 (P0): DSCI controller migrated to camelCase key names.\n68\t- HLR-3 (P0): service controller error logs include `resourceKind`.\n69\t- HLR-4 (P0): all 15 action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`.\n70\t- HLR-6 (P0): module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`.\n71\t- HLR-7 (P1, bundled): DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` — bundled because it is added in the same mechanical pass over the same `log.Error` call sites and verified by the same lint rule; not separately schedulable.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac8f88166758eb95","agent_id":"a50ea2e05f464d44a","session_id":"ddc88db0-c91c-4182-8c51-a0cdf64bc03d","uuid":"384a8ee3-0982-4e09-9e14-1e3934257685","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:35:18.754Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b425d8cff74d4afc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
