{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f018979f52fcfa5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: Document the structured log field convention and publish for external operator\n4\t  adoption\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: Documentation\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n14\tai_signals:\n15\t  change_specificity: 1\n16\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n17\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n18\t  existing_foundation: 1\n19\t  open_questions: 0\n20\t  external_dependency: -1\n21\t  human_process_gates: -1\n22\t  repo_access: 1\n23\t  architecture_claims: 1\n24\tinvestigation_signals: null\n25\tai_implementability: Medium\n26\tai_implementability_score: 2\n27\tjira_key: null\n28\tbranch: null\n29\tgated_by: null\n30\tgate_failure_impact: null\n31\t---\n32\t# Document the structured log field convention and publish for external operator adoption\n33\t\n34\t## Description\n35\t\n36\tThis epic produces the documentation deliverables of the strategy: a contribution guideline that specifies the structured log field convention for controller development in the rhods-operator, the design doc with the three-problem diagnosis and before/after code examples, the DSCI key-migration guide for operators, and publication of the convention for voluntary adoption by external operator teams (Cluster Observability Operator: Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) per platform policy overlay 0008.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\tContent outline (inside Scope per artifact contract):\n41\t\n42\t- **Contribution guideline** for new controller development in the rhods-operator, specifying:\n43\t  - Required structured fields: `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`.\n44\t  - camelCase field-naming rationale (alignment with controller-runtime's existing structured log key conventions).\n45\t  - The three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), missing `resourceKind`.\n46\t  - Cluster-scoped resource handling (namespace omitted or empty string).\n47\t  - How the CI lint rule enforces the convention.\n48\t- **Design doc** with before/after code examples for converting message-embedded resource identity to structured KV pairs (the strategy flags this doc as \"to be created\").\n49\t- **DSCI key-migration guide**: release-notes documentation of the migration from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to `name`/`namespace`, with before/after query examples for Loki/CloudWatch, noting the single-release transition intent.\n50\t- **External publication**: publish the convention as a specification for voluntary adoption by the COO-owned operators (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator), and file tracking issues in the COO projects. Adoption remains at the external teams' discretion per platform policy — RHOAI does not install, manage, or control external operator dependencies.\n51\t- **Open product decision to record in the guideline**: whether the convention extends beyond `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category) is a pending PM/Observability decision; the guideline documents the three required fields and marks extras as a future extension pending that decision.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- The contribution guideline exists, is committed to the rhods-operator repository, and specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis.\n56\t- The design doc includes before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured KV pairs and a DSCI key-migration guide with before/after query examples.\n57\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented conversion — a reviewer confirms the documented field names, examples, and controller-tier descriptions match the code as merged.\n58\t- Release notes document the DSCI key-name migration with before/after query examples.\n59\t- The convention is published as a specification for external operator adoption, and tracking issues are filed in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-8 (P1): document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac8f88166758eb95","agent_id":"a50ea2e05f464d44a","session_id":"ddc88db0-c91c-4182-8c51-a0cdf64bc03d","uuid":"b50458a6-c948-4088-87c0-b2ac1ae84f3a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:35:20.414Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f018979f52fcfa5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
